   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Pendulum Wave\n\nA row of pendulums drifts out of phase into waves, then snaps back into a straight line.\n\nCategory: backgrounds. Length: 15 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene needs a calm, hypnotic background loop that is clearly rule-based, with order dissolving into waves and snapping back into a line.\n- A section about timing, rhythm, sync or periodic systems needs a visual that shows phases drifting apart and realigning.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The loop should be a dense, organic texture rather than a row of distinct objects.\n- The scene needs a one-shot accent that fires and clears rather than a running loop: use trim-burst.\n\nVariables:\n- count (number, 2-40): Pendulums, default 15\n- cycles (number, 1-30): Cycles, default 10\n- loop_frames (number, 90-900): Loop length, default 450\n- background (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- color (color): Bobs, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- accent (color): Wave line, default \"#E5322D\"\n- show_guides (boolean): Guides, default true\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Pendulum Wave\n\n  A row of pendulums drifts out of phase into waves, then snaps back into a straight line.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/pendulum-wave/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"pendulum-wave\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"15\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\":\"count\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"layout\",\"label\":\"Pendulums\",\"description\":\"Number of pendulums in the row.\",\"default\":15,\"min\":2,\"max\":40,\"step\":1},{\"id\":\"cycles\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Cycles\",\"description\":\"Swings the slowest pendulum makes per loop; pendulum i makes cycles + i.\",\"default\":10,\"min\":1,\"max\":30,\"step\":1},{\"id\":\"loop_frames\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Loop length\",\"description\":\"Frames (at 30 fps) until every pendulum realigns.\",\"default\":450,\"min\":90,\"max\":900,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"frames\"},{\"id\":\"background\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Background\",\"description\":\"Backdrop color.\",\"default\":\"#111111\"},{\"id\":\"color\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Bobs\",\"description\":\"Color of the bobs and guides.\",\"default\":\"#FFFFFF\"},{\"id\":\"accent\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Wave line\",\"description\":\"Color of the line threaded through the bobs.\",\"default\":\"#E5322D\"},{\"id\":\"show_guides\",\"type\":\"boolean\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Guides\",\"description\":\"Draw the faint per-pendulum tracks and centre line.\",\"default\":true}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Pendulum Wave</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n\n        }\n        .pdw-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .pdw-svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"pendulum-wave\" data-duration=\"15\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"pdw-clip\" class=\"pdw-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"15\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg id=\"pdw-svg\" class=\"pdw-svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pendulum wave\"></svg>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Frame-based helpers, written from their definitions.\n            var Easing = (function () {\n              function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                    var u = 1 - t;\n                    var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (Math.abs(cx - x) < 1e-6) break;\n                    if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var v = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n              return {\n                bezier: bezier,\n                linear: function (t) { return t; },\n                quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n                cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n                sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n                poly: function (n) { return function (t) { return Math.pow(t, n); }; },\n                ease: bezier(0.42, 0, 1, 1),\n                out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n                inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; }\n              };\n            })();\n            function interpolate(input, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var left = o.extrapolateLeft || \"extend\";\n              var right = o.extrapolateRight || \"extend\";\n              var i = 1;\n              while (i < n - 1 && input > inR[i]) i++;\n              var a = inR[i - 1], b = inR[i];\n              if (input < inR[0] && left === \"clamp\") return outR[0];\n              if (input > inR[n - 1] && right === \"clamp\") return outR[n - 1];\n              var t = b === a ? 0 : (input - a) / (b - a);\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i - 1] + (outR[i] - outR[i - 1]) * t;\n            }\n            // Damped spring from rest to 1. durationInFrames stretches time so the spring has settled by then.\n            function spring(o) {\n              var c = o.config || {};\n              var mass = c.mass != null ? c.mass : 1;\n              var k = c.stiffness != null ? c.stiffness : 100;\n              var damp = c.damping != null ? c.damping : 10;\n              function at(t) {\n                var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / mass);\n                var z = damp / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * mass));\n                if (z < 1) {\n                  var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                  return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n                }\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              }\n              var t = Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.fps;\n              if (o.durationInFrames) {\n                var settle = 4, step = 1 / o.fps;\n                for (var s = settle; s > 0.05; s -= step) {\n                  if (Math.abs(1 - at(s)) > 0.001) { settle = s + step; break; }\n                  settle = s;\n                }\n                t = (Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.durationInFrames) * settle;\n                if (o.frame >= o.durationInFrames) return 1;\n              }\n              return at(t);\n            }\n            function parseColor(c) {\n              var m;\n              c = String(c).trim();\n              if ((m = /^#([0-9a-f]{3,8})$/i.exec(c))) {\n                var h = m[1];\n                if (h.length <= 4) h = h.split(\"\").map(function (x) { return x + x; }).join(\"\");\n                return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16), h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1];\n              }\n              if ((m = /^rgba?\\(([^)]+)\\)/i.exec(c))) {\n                var p = m[1].split(\",\").map(Number);\n                return [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.length > 3 ? p[3] : 1];\n              }\n              return [0, 0, 0, 1];\n            }\n            function interpolateColors(t, inR, outR) {\n              var a = parseColor(outR[0]), b = parseColor(outR[1]);\n              var u = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - inR[0]) / (inR[1] - inR[0])));\n              return \"rgba(\" + [0, 1, 2].map(function (i) { return Math.round(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u); }).join(\",\") + \",\" + (a[3] + (b[3] - a[3]) * u) + \")\";\n            }\n            // Seeded 0..1 value: the same seed always gives the same number.\n            function random(seed) {\n              var s = String(seed), h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n                h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n                h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 3266489917);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 15)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            // Fit a fixed-size design stage into the frame.\n            function fit(el, w, h, fill) {\n              var s = Math.min(root.clientWidth / w, root.clientHeight / h) * (fill || 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\";\n              el.style.left = \"50%\";\n              el.style.top = \"50%\";\n              el.style.width = w + \"px\";\n              el.style.height = h + \"px\";\n              el.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n            // Drive draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking always draws the same picture.\n            function clockTween(tl, totalFrames, draw, rate) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: totalFrames, duration: totalFrames / 30, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame * (rate || 1)); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n\n            var count = Math.round(num(vars.count, 15, 2, 40));\n            var cycles = num(vars.cycles, 10, 1, 30);\n            var loopFrames = Math.max(1, num(vars.loop_frames, 450, 90, 900));\n            var background = str(vars.background, \"#111111\");\n            var color = str(vars.color, \"#FFFFFF\");\n            var accent = str(vars.accent, \"#E5322D\");\n            var guides = bool(vars.show_guides, true);\n            root.style.background = background;\n\n            var TAU = Math.PI * 2, SMEAR_FRAMES = 4, SMEAR_SAMPLES = 6;\n            var width = root.clientWidth, height = root.clientHeight;\n            var svg = document.getElementById(\"pdw-svg\");\n            svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + width + \" \" + height);\n            var n = count;\n            var marginX = width * 0.1, gap = (width - marginX * 2) / (n - 1);\n            var amp = height * 0.3, cy = height / 2;\n            var r0 = Math.min(gap * 0.3, height * 0.022);\n            var unit = Math.min(width, height) / 720;\n            function fmt(v) { return Math.round(v * 10) / 10; }\n            function circle(x, y, r) {\n              return \"M \" + fmt(x - r) + \" \" + fmt(y) + \" a \" + fmt(r) + \" \" + fmt(r) + \" 0 1 0 \" + fmt(r * 2) + \" 0 a \" + fmt(r) + \" \" + fmt(r) + \" 0 1 0 \" + fmt(-r * 2) + \" 0\";\n            }\n            function smoothPath(p) {\n              var d = \"M \" + fmt(p[0].x) + \" \" + fmt(p[0].y);\n              for (var i = 0; i < p.length - 1; i++) {\n                var p0 = p[i - 1] || p[i], p1 = p[i], p2 = p[i + 1], p3 = p[i + 2] || p2;\n                d += \" C \" + fmt(p1.x + (p2.x - p0.x) / 6) + \" \" + fmt(p1.y + (p2.y - p0.y) / 6) + \" \" + fmt(p2.x - (p3.x - p1.x) / 6) + \" \" + fmt(p2.y - (p3.y - p1.y) / 6) + \" \" + fmt(p2.x) + \" \" + fmt(p2.y);\n              }\n              return d;\n            }\n            var bobsX = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) bobsX.push(marginX + i * gap);\n            if (guides) {\n              var g = svgEl(\"g\", { stroke: color, fill: \"none\" }, svg);\n              svgEl(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + fmt(marginX - gap) + \" \" + cy + \" H \" + fmt(width - marginX + gap), \"stroke-opacity\": 0.14, \"stroke-width\": unit }, g);\n              svgEl(\"path\", { d: bobsX.map(function (x) { return \"M \" + fmt(x) + \" \" + fmt(cy - amp) + \" V \" + fmt(cy + amp); }).join(\" \"), \"stroke-opacity\": 0.08, \"stroke-width\": unit, \"stroke-dasharray\": 2 * unit + \" \" + 6 * unit }, g);\n              svgEl(\"path\", { d: bobsX.map(function (x) { return circle(x, cy - amp, 2.2 * unit) + \" \" + circle(x, cy + amp, 2.2 * unit); }).join(\" \"), fill: color, \"fill-opacity\": 0.25, stroke: \"none\" }, g);\n            }\n            var wave = svgEl(\"path\", { fill: \"none\", stroke: accent, \"stroke-width\": 2.5 * unit, \"stroke-linecap\": \"round\", \"stroke-opacity\": 0.85 }, svg);\n            var smearEl = svgEl(\"path\", { fill: \"none\", stroke: color, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.13, \"stroke-width\": r0 * 0.9, \"stroke-linecap\": \"round\", \"stroke-linejoin\": \"round\" }, svg);\n            var bobEl = svgEl(\"path\", { fill: color }, svg);\n\n            function phaseAt(i, t) { return (TAU * t * (cycles + i)) / loopFrames; }\n            function draw(time) {\n              var bobs = [], smear = \"\";\n              for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                var c = Math.cos(phaseAt(i, time));\n                bobs.push({ x: bobsX[i], y: cy - amp * c, r: r0 * (1 - 0.22 * c) });\n              }\n              for (var j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                var x = fmt(bobsX[j]);\n                for (var s = 0; s <= SMEAR_SAMPLES; s++) {\n                  var t = time - (SMEAR_FRAMES * s) / SMEAR_SAMPLES;\n                  smear += (s === 0 ? \"M\" : \"L\") + \" \" + x + \" \" + fmt(cy - amp * Math.cos(phaseAt(j, t))) + \" \";\n                }\n              }\n              wave.setAttribute(\"d\", smoothPath(bobs));\n              smearEl.setAttribute(\"d\", smear);\n              bobEl.setAttribute(\"d\", bobs.map(function (b) { return circle(b.x, b.y, b.r); }).join(\" \"));\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            clockTween(tl, 450, draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"15\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"pendulum-wave\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
